; wordskin-native-ingest.fk — how much of a wordskin can the body swallow natively?
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk
;
; Source: "Robert Edward Grant LIVE | Elevating Consciousness | 'The Knowledge
; Graph'" (youtu.be/aprhb2wonGQ), full auto-caption transcript read 2026-08-17.
; Corpus row 1027 (offered as 1015, renumbered at the 2026-08-19
; reunion) named the material: a wordskin — a claim wearing this body's
; words (coherence, harmonic, knowledge graph) without this body's proofs.
;
; The experiment (Urs, 2026-08-17): how much can we ingest using 100% native
; form query validation? The seam is held honestly: the RENTED mind extracted
; and encoded the claims (that sorting is not native and is not claimed to be);
; every VERDICT below is computed by the body itself — integer arithmetic only,
; no floats, no division (cross-multiplication), roots held in squared terms.
;
; Lanes (extended 2026-08-17 same evening — Urs: a missing stone is a signal
; for repair, not a stopper; and push every pending claim to its true depth):
;   A  native-arithmetic           — the body decides outright             (c1-c17)
;   B  native-over-cited-constants — the body computes, constants cited    (c16, c18-c21, c28)
;   D  shape-decided               — the claim's internal STRUCTURE gets a
;                                    native verdict; its empirical data is
;                                    absent and stays pending              (c22-c28)
;   E  external-witnessed          — verified against a named external
;                                    source; no native computation exists
;                                    in this body yet (no ephemeris), so
;                                    cited, never verdicted natively       (p7a)
;   C  pending-irreducible         — cannot be encoded falsifiably; listed,
;                                    counted, never verdicted (honest pending)
;
; The lt witness (this same evening): c14/c15 first shipped with gt-swaps
; because the writer had not SEEN lt in the body and routed around it. Probed:
; (lt 1 2) answers native on fkwu, and "lt" is bound in the Go (jit.go AND
; bp_table.go — both sides of the JIT ABI mirror), Rust, and TS kernel sources.
; The stone was in the wall on all four arms; only the witnessing was missing.
; c14/c15 below now stand on lt as the mathematics reads.
;
; Cited constants (lane B, external ground, named so the seam is visible):
;   Great Pyramid base 230.36 m -> perimeter 92144 cm (survey, Petrie lineage)
;   Great Pyramid original height 146.60 m -> 14660 cm
;   Earth polar circumference 40,007,860 m -> 4000786000 cm
;   Earth polar radius 6,356,752 m -> 635675200 cm
;   Hebrew letter values (Mispar Hechrachi): tav 400, bet 2, lamed 30
;
; Verdict fold: bit i (power of two) set iff claim i holds AS GRANT STATED IT.
; A cleared bit is also a successful ingest — the body reached a verdict of
; refuted. Only lane C is a failure to ingest. 28 checks -> full field
; 268435455, far under the 2^53 fold ceiling. Witnessed run 2026-08-17:
; verdict-bits 251002879 = full field minus c18 (2^17), c20 (2^19), c25 (2^24)
; — the two "exactly 43,200x" claims and the 2000x-vs-own-2%-premise claim.
;
; Former pending ledger, each pushed to its true verification depth:
;   p1  72 Hz "unstruck root" of all pyramids     -> lane D, c27: the stated
;       tonic 432 IS in the 72-series (432 = 6*72) — root/tonic mutually
;       consistent; per-pyramid frequencies still unpublished (data pending)
;   p2  Kukulcan/Teotihuacan/Khufu = A-minor      -> lane D, c26: a minor triad
;       10:12:15 IS realizable among integer multiples of 72 (720:864:1080 =
;       partials 10,12,15) — the two claims are compatible in shape; his
;       specific pyramid frequencies still unstated (data pending)
;   p3  raised mark on pyramid reads 5,4,3,2,[1]  — lane C: interpretive, no test
;   p4  davar -> tevel via D>T, B>V(same letter), R>L -> lane D, c23: the swap
;       is mechanically consistent as a letter map (d b r) -> (t b l); its
;       LINGUISTIC validity has no encoding (that part stays pending)
;   p5  half-side construction forces Riemann line -> lane D, c22: the true
;       kernel inside the claim — the only fixed point of the zeta symmetry
;       s <-> 1-s is s = 1/2 — verdicts native. That the SPIRAL forces zeros
;       there has no encoding and stays pending
;   p6  "OA solved dark matter / aging"           — lane C: unfalsifiable as stated
;   p7  Om chant activates pyramids               — lane C: unfalsifiable; BUT its
;       sub-claim p7a (total eclipse 2027-08-02, ~6 min) is lane E: NASA GSFC
;       SE2027Aug02Tgoogle.html, fetched 2026-08-17, witnesses "Total Solar
;       Eclipse of 2027 Aug 02", greatest duration 06m23.2s. (The Luxor-path
;       detail was not in the fetched text and is NOT claimed here.) This body
;       holds no ephemeris, so no native verdict — cited, not folded.
;   p8  Mount Meru = Great Pyramid                — lane C: interpretive identification
;   p9  100x-2000x inference energy claim         -> lane D, c24/c25: given HIS
;       premise (2% of queries need LLM inference), the saving ceiling is
;       100/2 = 50x — so "about 50x" is exactly the ceiling of his own
;       mechanism (c24 upholds consistency), while "up to 2000x" exceeds that
;       ceiling 40-fold (c25 refutes it against his own stated premise)
;   p10 underwater pyramids (Bali, Scotland)      -> lane D, c28: his two
;       descriptions of the second rock ("5-12-13 proportion", "67.38 degree
;       angle") are ONE claim — tan = 12/5 = 2.4, and atan(12/5) = 67.380
;       degrees (cited constant); shape-consistent. Whether the rock is a
;       built pyramid remains empirical and pending.

(do
    (defn wni-bit (cond bit) (if cond bit 0))

    ; --- lane A: native arithmetic ---
    ; c1/c2 tetraktys: 4+3+2+1 = 10, 4*3*2*1 = 24
    (defn wni-c1 () (eq (add 4 (add 3 (add 2 1))) 10))
    (defn wni-c2 () (eq (mul 4 (mul 3 (mul 2 1))) 24))
    ; c3 (10,24,26) is a right triangle
    (defn wni-c3 () (eq (add (mul 10 10) (mul 24 24)) (mul 26 26)))
    ; c4 (10,24,26) is exactly 2x(5,12,13)
    (defn wni-c4 () (and (eq 10 (mul 2 5)) (and (eq 24 (mul 2 12)) (eq 26 (mul 2 13)))))
    ; c5 (5,12,13) is a right triangle
    (defn wni-c5 () (eq (add (mul 5 5) (mul 12 12)) (mul 13 13)))
    ; c6 arithmetic mean of {0,1} is 1/2:  (0+1)/2 = 1/2  <=>  (0+1)*2 = 1*2
    (defn wni-c6 () (eq (mul (add 0 1) 2) (mul 1 2)))
    ; c7 geometric mean of {0,1} is 0:  sqrt(0*1) = 0  held squared: 0*1 = 0*0
    (defn wni-c7 () (eq (mul 0 1) (mul 0 0)))
    ; c8 difference mean (1-0)/2 is 1/2  <=>  (1-0)*2 = 1*2
    (defn wni-c8 () (eq (mul (sub 1 0) 2) (mul 1 2)))
    ; c9 sides (1/2, 1/2, 0) cannot close — triangle inequality fails, as he
    ;    stated. In halves: NOT (1 + 0 > 1).
    (defn wni-c9 () (if (gt (add 1 0) 1) false true))
    ; c10 the 1D Pythagorean test fails, as he stated: (1/2)^2+(1/2)^2 != 0^2.
    ;     In quarters: 1+1 != 0.
    (defn wni-c10 () (if (eq (add 1 1) 0) false true))
    ; c11 legs 1/2,1/2 give hyp^2 = 1/2: quarters 1+1=2, and 2/4 = 1/2 <=> 2*2 = 4*1
    (defn wni-c11 () (and (eq (add 1 1) 2) (eq (mul 2 2) (mul 4 1))))
    ; c12 spiral recurrence: (1/2)^2 + (sqrt(n)/2)^2 = (sqrt(n+1)/2)^2 — in
    ;     quarters, 1+n = n+1 for each stated step (n = 2, 3, 4).
    (defn wni-c12-step (n) (eq (add 1 n) (add n 1)))
    (defn wni-c12 () (and (wni-c12-step 2) (and (wni-c12-step 3) (wni-c12-step 4))))
    ; c13 step-n tangent: (outer/inner)^2 * n = 1 with outer 1, inner sqrt(n):
    ;     (1/n)*n = 1  <=>  n = n, checked at n = 2, 3, 10.
    (defn wni-c13-step (n) (eq (mul 1 n) (mul n 1)))
    (defn wni-c13 () (and (wni-c13-step 2) (and (wni-c13-step 3) (wni-c13-step 10))))
    ; c14 for 0 < x < 1 (x = 93/100): 0 < x^2 < x — squaring shrinks toward the
    ;     zero floor, never below.  x^2 < x  <=>  a*a*b < a*b*b.
    (defn wni-c14 ()
        (and (gt (mul 93 93) 0)
             (lt (mul (mul 93 93) 100) (mul 93 (mul 100 100)))))
    ; c15 for x > 1 (x = 93/10): 1 < sqrt(x) < x  <=>  x < x^2  <=>  b < a.
    (defn wni-c15 () (lt 10 93))
    ; c16 gematria of tevel: tav 400 + bet 2 + lamed 30 = 432 (values cited above)
    (defn wni-c16 () (eq (add 400 (add 2 30)) 432))
    ; c17 43200 is a base-60 round number: 12 * 60 * 60
    (defn wni-c17 () (eq (mul 12 (mul 60 60)) 43200))

    ; --- lane B: native computation over cited constants (all in cm) ---
    (defn wni-perimeter-scaled () (mul 92144 43200))
    (defn wni-earth-circumference () 4000786000)
    (defn wni-height-scaled () (mul 14660 43200))
    (defn wni-earth-radius () 635675200)
    (defn wni-gap (a b) (if (gt a b) (sub a b) (sub b a)))
    ; c18 "the perimeter is a 43,200x EXACT scale model of the polar circumference"
    (defn wni-c18 () (eq (wni-perimeter-scaled) (wni-earth-circumference)))
    ; c19 ...but it IS within 10 per-mille:  gap*1000 <= 10*b
    (defn wni-c19 ()
        (le (mul (wni-gap (wni-perimeter-scaled) (wni-earth-circumference)) 1000)
            (mul 10 (wni-earth-circumference))))
    ; c20 "the height is EXACTLY the polar radius / 43,200"
    (defn wni-c20 () (eq (wni-height-scaled) (wni-earth-radius)))
    ; c21 ...but it IS within 10 per-mille
    (defn wni-c21 ()
        (le (mul (wni-gap (wni-height-scaled) (wni-earth-radius)) 1000)
            (mul 10 (wni-earth-radius))))

    ; --- lane D: shape verdicts on the former pending claims ---
    ; c22 (p5) the only fixed point of s <-> 1-s is 1/2. In halves (s = x/2):
    ;     x = 2-x holds at x=1 and at no probed neighbor.
    (defn wni-c22 ()
        (and (eq 1 (sub 2 1))
             (and (if (eq 0 (sub 2 0)) false true)
                  (if (eq 2 (sub 2 2)) false true))))
    ; c23 (p4) the letter swap is mechanically consistent: d->t, b->b, r->l
    ;     applied to (d b r) yields (t b l).
    (defn wni-swap (letter)
        (if (str_eq letter "d") "t"
            (if (str_eq letter "r") "l" letter)))
    (defn wni-swap-all (letters)
        (if (nil? letters) letters
            (cons (wni-swap (head letters)) (wni-swap-all (tail letters)))))
    (defn wni-list-eq (a b)
        (if (eq (len a) (len b))
            (if (eq (len a) 0) true
                (if (str_eq (head a) (head b)) (wni-list-eq (tail a) (tail b)) false))
            false))
    (defn wni-c23 ()
        (wni-list-eq (wni-swap-all (list "d" "b" "r")) (list "t" "b" "l")))
    ; c24 (p9) with 2% of queries needing LLM inference, the saving ceiling is
    ;     100/2 = 50x — his "about 50 times" is the ceiling of his own premise.
    (defn wni-c24 () (eq (mul 2 50) 100))
    ; c25 (p9) "up to 2000x" from the same 2% premise: needs 2000 <= 50.
    ;     The body answers this one directly.
    (defn wni-c25 () (le 2000 50))
    ; c26 (p2) a minor triad 10:12:15 is realizable among integer multiples of
    ;     72: 720, 864, 1080 are partials 10, 12, 15 and hold the triad ratios.
    (defn wni-c26 ()
        (and (eq 720 (mul 10 72))
        (and (eq 864 (mul 12 72))
        (and (eq 1080 (mul 15 72))
        (and (eq (mul 720 12) (mul 864 10))
             (eq (mul 720 15) (mul 1080 10)))))))
    ; c27 (p1) the stated tonic sits in the stated root's series: 432 = 6*72.
    (defn wni-c27 () (eq (mul 6 72) 432))
    ; c28 (p10) "5-12-13 proportion" and "67.38 degrees" are one claim:
    ;     tan = 12/5 = 24/10, and atan(12/5) = 67.380 degrees (cited constant).
    (defn wni-c28 () (eq (mul 12 10) (mul 24 5)))

    ; --- fold: power-of-two bit weights, bit set iff the claim held as stated ---
    (defn wni-verdict-bits ()
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c1) 1)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c2) 2)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c3) 4)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c4) 8)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c5) 16)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c6) 32)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c7) 64)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c8) 128)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c9) 256)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c10) 512)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c11) 1024)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c12) 2048)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c13) 4096)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c14) 8192)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c15) 16384)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c16) 32768)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c17) 65536)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c18) 131072)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c19) 262144)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c20) 524288)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c21) 1048576)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c22) 2097152)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c23) 4194304)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c24) 8388608)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c25) 16777216)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c26) 33554432)
        (add (wni-bit (wni-c27) 67108864)
             (wni-bit (wni-c28) 134217728)))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
    (defn wni-one (cond) (if cond 1 0))
    (defn wni-upheld-count ()
        (add (wni-one (wni-c1))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c2))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c3))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c4))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c5))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c6))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c7))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c8))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c9))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c10))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c11))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c12))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c13))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c14))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c15))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c16))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c17))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c18))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c19))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c20))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c21))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c22))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c23))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c24))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c25))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c26))
        (add (wni-one (wni-c27))
             (wni-one (wni-c28))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))

    ; readout: 21 full-native + 7 shape checks over 6 former-pending claims;
    ; 1 external-witnessed (p7a, cited not folded); 3 pending-irreducible
    ; (p3 p6 p8). 21 + 6 + 1 + 3 = 31 extracted.
    (list (list "claims-extracted" 31)
          (list "full-native" 21)
          (list "shape-decided" 6)
          (list "external-witnessed" 1)
          (list "pending-irreducible" 3)
          (list "verdict-bits" (wni-verdict-bits))
          (list "checks" 28)
          (list "upheld" (wni-upheld-count))
          (list "refuted" (sub 28 (wni-upheld-count)))))
